---
/**
 * Hero: choose an area on NAIP aerial imagery and get that patch as an array.
 * Composition bitmap has no titles/captions; chrome lives here.
 */
---

<figure class="ta-fig ta-fig--wide">
  <div class="ta-fig__chrome">
    <p class="ta-fig__eyebrow">FIG. 01</p>
    <p class="ta-fig__title">From an area on the map to pixels in Python</p>
    <p class="ta-fig__lede">
      Aerial imagery over San Francisco Bay. The rust box marks the area of interest;
      the second panel is that same display crop as an array — ready to inspect or pass into a model.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="ta-fig__frame">
    <picture>
      <source
        media="(max-width: 640px)"
        srcset="/images/tilearray/fig01-hero-mobile.webp"
      />
      <img
        class="ta-fig__img"
        src="/images/tilearray/fig01-hero-desktop.webp"
        alt="Side-by-side view: NAIP aerial mosaic of the Golden Gate with a rust area-of-interest box, linked to the extracted patch shown as a georeferenced array."
        width="1400"
        height="720"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </picture>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="ta-fig__caption">
    USGS / USDA NAIP NaturalColor (public domain). The rust box is an illustrative display crop for the story —
    TileArray’s default mosaic follows the covering tile grid and may extend beyond a drawn AOI.
    Mosaic seams in the water are from assembling adjacent image tiles.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .ta-fig {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .ta-fig--wide {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: none;
    margin-left: 0;
  }

  .ta-fig__chrome {
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .ta-fig__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.2rem;
    color: var(--colour-rust);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .ta-fig__title {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .ta-fig__lede {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--colour-muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .ta-fig__frame {
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-rule);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--colour-paper) 92%, var(--colour-blue));
    padding: 0.55rem;
  }

  .ta-fig__img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .ta-fig__caption {
    margin: 0.65rem 0 0;
    color: var(--colour-muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }
</style>
